		(uuid "d4c3477d-7f76-5929-9cbe-328e5bb97d93")
	)
	(text "Power flow: J101 24 V (30 V max) -> F101 3 A -> VM. Q101 (low-side N-FET) blocks a reversed input; D101 SMAJ33A\nclamps VM. VM feeds the bridges (sheet 3) and U201, the 5 V buck (sheet 2). 5V_BUCK and USB VBUS are OR-ed by\nD201/D202 into +5V; U202 makes +3V3. VDDA is +3V3 through R401 (0 ohm, ferrite option).\n\nGrounding: one ground net (GND) on two solid inner planes (In1, In2). VIN_N (the input minus before Q101) is the\nonly other return and carries the input current only. The USB shield is tied to GND (D-008).\n\nPower and ground table\n  net       voltage            source                 class\n  VIN_RAW   24 V nom, 30 V max  J101.1                 PWR_3A\n  VIN_N     0 V (input minus)   J101.2 -> Q101         PWR_3A\n  VM        24 V nom, 30 V max  F101 (after the fuse)  PWR_3A\n  5V_BUCK   5.0 V               U201 (LMR36510)        PWR_1A\n  VBUS      5 V (USB)           J601                   PWR_1A\n  +5V       4.5-4.8 V           D201 / D202            PWR_1A\n  +3V3      3.3 V               U202 (AP2112K)         PWR_0p5A\n  VDDA      3.3 V               R401 from +3V3         PWR_0p5A\n  VFBSMPS   1.4-1.9 V           U401 SMPS              PWR_0p5A\n  GND       0 V                 planes In1/In2         GND\n\nSpare and not-fitted parts: C501, C502 (antenna tuning shunts) are DNP, fitted at bring-up with a VNA (D-007).\nR501 0 ohm is the series element of that pi. R401 0 ohm can become a ferrite (D-020). No unused gates.\nNumbering: sheet n holds references n01-n99. Sheets: 1 input, 2 supplies, 3 motor, 4 MCU, 5 radio, 6 USB, 7 UI."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 246.38 0)
